.TH HITSIDE 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
HitSide \- Which side of rectangle b rectangle a struck, as reported by rect_hit_side(): the side of b that a came from
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqcollide.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef enum { HIT_LEFT, HIT_RIGHT, HIT_TOP, HIT_BOTTOM } HitSide;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Which side of rectangle b rectangle a struck, as reported by rect_hit_side(): the side of b that a came from. HIT_TOP means a landed on top of b (a is above), HIT_BOTTOM that a hit b from below, HIT_LEFT that a is to the left of b, HIT_RIGHT to the right.
.SH VALUES
.TP
.B HIT_LEFT
a came from the left of b
.TP
.B HIT_RIGHT
a came from the right of b
.TP
.B HIT_TOP
a came from above b (landed on it)
.TP
.B HIT_BOTTOM
a came from below b (bumped its underside)
.SH MODULE
math (src/engine/math/collide.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rect_hit_side (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
